# PLAN-937 CA-D1 T-09: the scalar bridge corpus (source export + typed
# peers + negatives). The source leg compiles REAL Auto source through
# the checked frontdoor into the public C library and EXECUTES it with
# the independent hand-written caller; the typed legs run the frozen
# typed declarations across the real machine-code peers.

# Source export: cold publish (facts+plan+2 fragments+library), pure
# second-query hit (zero producers).
```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace-ca-d1.source-export"
  tags: ["ca-d1", "probe"]
  source: { file: "src/bridge-source.atomdata", syntax: "atom-data", path: "bridge-source.atomdata" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "source-export", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: {
        recipe: "abi/ca-d1-bridge-v1",
        abi: { leg: "source" },
        steps: [ { op: "query" }, { op: "query" } ]
      },
      expect: { completion: "success", probe: [
        { cache: "published", compute_calls: 5, stages_include: ["bridge"] },
        { cache: "hit", compute_calls: 0 }
      ] } }
  ]
}
```

# Body edit (the distinguishing oracle): the +1 edit flips the DELIVERED
# value; the frozen independent caller (hand-computed 42) must FAIL the
# PE — completion run/pe-exit, never a wrong native pass. Republish
# count = facts + the edited sum fragment + library (plan is a pure hit).
```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace-ca-d1.source-body-edit"
  tags: ["ca-d1", "probe", "negative"]
  source: { file: "src/bridge-source.atomdata", syntax: "atom-data", path: "bridge-source.atomdata" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "source-body-edit", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: {
        recipe: "abi/ca-d1-bridge-v1",
        abi: { leg: "source" },
        steps: [
          { op: "edit-source", from: "return a + b }", to: "return a + b + 1 }" },
          { op: "query" },
          { op: "query" }
        ]
      },
      expect: { completion: { stage: "run", code: "pe-exit" }, probe: [
        { cache: "published", compute_calls: 5 },
        { cache: "hit", compute_calls: 0 }
      ] } }
  ]
}
```

# Typed peers: each leg's first query produces the typed bridge
# artifacts (facts+plan+callee, plus the cside C object on the cross
# legs), the second query is a pure hit.
```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ace-ca-d1.typed-self"
  tags: ["ca-d1", "probe"]
  source: { file: "src/bridge-typed.atomdata", syntax: "atom-data", path: "bridge-typed.atomdata" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "typed-self", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: {
        recipe: "abi/ca-d1-bridge-v1",
        abi: { leg: "typed-self" },
        steps: [ { op: "query" }, { op: "query" } ]
      },
      expect: { completion: "success", probe: [
        { cache: "published", compute_calls: 3 },
        { cache: "hit", compute_calls: 0 }
      ] } }
  ]
}
```

